      "mergedPostDetails": "Title: YouTube videos fail on my client while others in the same world can watch\n\nPlatform: PC, Desktop mode\n\nRegion: Alberta, Canada\n\nISP: MCSnet\n\nVRChat build: 1681\n\nGPU/Driver: Nvidia 32.0.15.8097\n\nWindows: 11\n\nSummary:\n\nTwitch and other sources play normally, but YouTube videos fail only on my client. Friends in the same world can watch videos but when I try to input a link it breaks the player for everyone.\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\n1) Join any world that uses a YouTube player (tested multiple worlds)\n\n2) Paste a YouTube URL that others can watch\n\n3) I get \"Video Error\" on my side, others see it play\n\nExpected:\n\nShared YouTube videos should resolve and play for all clients.\n\nActual:\n\nLog shows yt-dlp is called correctly, then YouTube rejects it:\n\nERROR: [youtube] <id>: The following content is not available on this app.. Watch on the latest version of YouTube.\n\nProcess exits code 1. AVPro then fails to open the source.\n\nWhat I have tried:\n\n- Clear cache and PlayerPrefs\n\n- Delete AppData\\LocalLow\\VRChat\\VRChat entirely\n\n- Full reinstall\n\n- Flush DNS, reboot router\n\n- Firewall and AV exclusions, Defender off for test\n\n- Tested multiple worlds\n\nNotes:\n\nTwitch runs fine on the same worlds and session. This looks YouTube specific to my client rather than world setup or general connectivity.",
